# What gcloud uploads to the Cloud Build staging bucket when deploy_gcp.sh runs
# `gcloud run deploy --source backend`.
#
# Without this file gcloud ships the whole directory. The root .gitignore does not
# save you: gcloud looks for an ignore file in the SOURCE directory, and backend/
# has no .gitignore of its own.
#
# WHAT STAYS OUT, and why each one matters:
#   .env                  live Odoo and PEAK UAT credentials — API key, passwords, token
#   var/master_sheet.txt  the source sheet, carrying phone numbers BEFORE masking
#   .venv                 44 MB the image never uses; the Dockerfile pip installs
#                         from requirements.txt
#
# WHAT GOES, and why it is not an oversight:
#   static/                the built interface. The Dockerfile's `COPY stati[c] ./static`
#                           needs it, or the deploy serves an API with no interface.
#
# `var/*` and not `var/`: any NEW file dropped into var/ stays excluded by default,
# which is the safe direction for a folder that has held raw personal data. (The
# Odoo snapshot file it once re-included went with the sale.order sync, 2026-09-25.)

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

var/*

.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.git
.gcloudignore
